    "raw": "\\*Enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-2000 K:</td><td> $Cp^o$  = 18.814 + 0.634 $\\times$ 10 $^{-3}$ T - 3.480 $\\times$ 10 $^5$ T $^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o$ -  $H_{298}^o$  = 18.814 $\\times$ 10 $^{-3}$ T + 0.317 $\\times$ 10 $^{-6}$ T $^2$  + 3.480 $\\times$ 10 $^2$ T $^{-1}$  - 6.805</td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-2000 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -127.781 + 1.963 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 0.177 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 179.200 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -127.781 - 1.963 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T + 0.177 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 89.600 \\text{T}^{-1} + 47.039 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr></table>\nSource: Data from Pankratz (92). ",
